// An engine limit, not a language rule. §3.3 Table 3-3 lets a replication
// multiply a string by any non-negative count. A replication whose count is
// known only at run time builds its text in a 4096-byte buffer and ends the
// run past it (E1011); one whose count and text fold is refused past the same
// 4096 bytes when the model compiles (docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md), so the two
// agree. {5000{"x"}} is 5000 bytes. A count of 10^12 used to exhaust memory
// while folding.
//
// Legal neighbour: string_replication_4096_bytes.va.
//
//! reject E1011
//! reject the replication makes 5000 copies of 1 bytes
module string_replication_over_4096_bytes_rejected(p, n);
  inout p, n; electrical p, n;
  string s;
  analog begin
    s = {5000{"x"}};
    I(p, n) <+ V(p, n) * (s == "");
  end
endmodule
